00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:33,940
edematosynovium,
inflammatory cells,

260
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:37,160
granulation tissue
and fibroblasts

261
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:39,580
that grow over
the articular

262
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:41,380
cartilage and erodes it.

263
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:44,520
These elements are
very nicely represented

264
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:47,740
in these two
histological images.

265
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:51,580
After destruction
of cartilage, the

266
00:14:51,580 --> 00:14:56,320
panus bridges and
the opposing bones

267
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:59,380
form a fibrous
ankylosis, which may

268
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:02,200
ossify and result
in bone fusion.

269
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:05,880
Ultimately, there
is bony ankylosis.

270
00:15:08,220 --> 00:15:10,580
In rheumatoid
arthritis there is

271
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:12,580
a symmetric joint
involvement.

272
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:16,100
The joints at the
hand level, except

273
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:19,280
the distal
interphalangeal joint, the

274
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:21,680
wrists, the hips,
the knees, cervical

275
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:23,820
spine, the feet, the
ankles, the elbows

276
00:15:23,820 --> 00:15:26,640
and shoulders are
usually involved

277
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:29,940
The pain is usually
worse in the morning

278
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:32,620
The patients
would also present

279
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:34,340
with systemic
symptoms such as

280
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:36,320
fever, fatigue
and weight loss

281
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:39,400
Laboratory investigation
is very important

282
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:42,480
to confirm the
diagnosis The most

283
00:15:42,480 --> 00:15:46,860
specific and sensitive
test is the anti-CCP.

284
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,900
The patients with
rheumatoid arthritis

285
00:15:49,900 --> 00:15:53,600
present also with
an elevated ESR, an

286
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:57,300
elevated CRP and a
positive RF titer.

287
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:01,380
If you examine the
joint fluid, you'll

288
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:03,600
see that the complement
is decreased.

289
00:16:14,930 --> 00:16:16,810
On this slide, I
thought it's a good idea

290
00:16:16,810 --> 00:16:19,830
to insist on hand
findings in patients with

291
00:16:19,830 --> 00:16:24,650
rheumatoid arthritis.
So, there are Bouchard

292
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:27,950
nodes in these patients.
These are described

293
00:16:27,950 --> 00:16:30,450
at the proximo
-enterpharyngeal joint.

294
00:16:30,870 --> 00:16:33,990
However, there
are no Heberdine

295
00:16:33,990 --> 00:16:36,930
nodes, but we can see

296
00:16:36,930 --> 00:16:39,230
inflammation in
tendons, ligaments,

297
00:16:39,570 --> 00:16:41,730
sometimes adjacent
skeletal muscle

298
00:16:41,730 --> 00:16:44,450
produces radial
deviation of the wrist,

299
00:16:45,030 --> 00:16:46,910
ulnar deviation
of fingers,

300
00:16:47,230 --> 00:16:49,330
and flexion
hyperextension

301
00:16:49,330 --> 00:16:51,930
fingers, the so
-called swan neck

302
00:16:51,930 --> 00:16:54,090
and boutonniere
deformities.

303
00:16:57,810 --> 00:17:00,310
Rheumatoid arthritis
is also characterized

304
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:02,890
by a development of
rheumatoid nodules

305
00:17:02,890 --> 00:17:05,130
outside the joints,
for example in the

306
00:17:05,130 --> 00:17:08,010
subcutaneous tissue
of forearm, elbows,

307
00:17:08,010 --> 00:17:10,910
occiput and lumbosacral
area, the areas of

308
00:17:10,910 --> 00:17:14,450
pressure. On evaluation,
these are small,

309
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:17,030
firm, non-tender,
round to oval masses.

310
00:17:17,510 --> 00:17:19,630
Rheumatoid nodules
are described in

311
00:17:19,630 --> 00:17:22,690
the lungs, and in
this case the patients

312
00:17:22,690 --> 00:17:24,750
are diagnosed with
Kaplan syndrome.

313
00:17:25,270 --> 00:17:27,740
Histological evaluation
of these lesions

314
00:17:27,740 --> 00:17:31,050
will show, as you can
see in this histological

315
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:34,690
image, necrotizing
granulomas with central

316
00:17:34,690 --> 00:17:37,210
zone of fibrinoid
necrosis surrounded by

317
00:17:37,210 --> 00:17:39,930
prominent ream of
palisading activated

318
00:17:39,930 --> 00:17:43,330
macrophages, many
lymphocytes and plasma cells.

319
00:17:43,650 --> 00:17:46,910
Severe rheumatoid
arthritis may be associated

320
00:17:46,910 --> 00:17:49,910
with acute necrotizing
vasculitis of

321
00:17:49,910 --> 00:17:52,230
small and large arteries
which may involve

322
00:17:52,230 --> 00:17:55,490
the pleura, the
pericardium or the lung.

323
00:17:55,690 --> 00:17:58,990
This in turn will
produce purpura,

324
00:17:58,990 --> 00:18:02,630
cutaneous ulcers and
nile bed infarction.

325
00:18:02,850 --> 00:18:05,910
Ocular changes
in rheumatoid

326
00:18:05,910 --> 00:18:09,010
arthritis are
represented by uveitis,

327
00:18:09,010 --> 00:18:12,190
scleritis and
keratoconjunctivitis.

328
00:18:12,450 --> 00:18:14,880
There is also
interstitial

329
00:18:14,930 --> 00:18:16,970
lung disease in
some patients.

330
00:18:17,150 --> 00:18:19,190
Some other patients
will present

331
00:18:19,190 --> 00:18:21,410
with pericarditis, anemia

332
00:18:21,530 --> 00:18:23,130
of chronic disease.

333
00:18:23,350 --> 00:18:26,250
There is also a Felty
syndrome described

334
00:18:26,250 --> 00:18:28,550
in these patients
which is associated

335
00:18:28,710 --> 00:18:31,490
with neutropenia
and splenomegaly.

336
00:18:34,010 --> 00:18:37,910
This slide summarizes
the most important

337
00:18:37,910 --> 00:18:40,170
differences between
osteoarthritis

338
00:18:40,170 --> 00:18:42,730
and rheumatoid
arthritis. Osteoarthritis

339
00:18:42,730 --> 00:18:45,790
is mechanical slash
degenerative, whereas

340
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:47,770
rheumatoid arthritis
is autoimmune.

341
00:18:47,910 --> 00:18:50,330
Osteoarthritis is
characterized by

342
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:52,690
cartilage degeneration
and fragmentation,

343
00:18:52,830 --> 00:18:55,330
bone spurs,
subchondral cysts,

344
00:18:55,330 --> 00:18:56,590
and minimal inflammation.

345
00:18:56,750 --> 00:19:00,090
The rheumatoid arthritis
is associated with

346
00:19:00,090 --> 00:19:02,630
inflammatory panels
which invades and

347
00:19:02,630 --> 00:19:05,610
destroys the cartilage
there is severe chronic

348
00:19:05,610 --> 00:19:10,630
inflammation and ankylosis
so the inflammation

349
00:19:10,630 --> 00:19:12,690
in osteoarthritis
is secondary whereas

350
00:19:12,690 --> 00:19:16,220
in rheumatoid arthritis
is primary osteoarthritis

351
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:19,350
is worse with
activity whereas the

352
00:19:19,350 --> 00:19:22,690
rheumatoid arthritis
is worse upon waking up

353
00:19:22,690 --> 00:19:26,970
in terms of location
osteoarthritis is

354
00:19:26,970 --> 00:19:29,910
asymmetric initially with
weight-bearing joints

355
00:19:29,910 --> 00:19:32,470
being involved of
course the hands are

356
00:19:32,470 --> 00:19:35,970
involved as well while
the rheumatoid arthritis

357
00:19:35,970 --> 00:19:38,970
is a symmetric
condition which starts

358
00:19:38,970 --> 00:19:42,770
initially in the hands
and feet the laboratory

359
00:19:42,770 --> 00:19:45,290
investigations shows
a non-inflammatory

360
00:19:45,290 --> 00:19:48,330
aspirate in osteoarthritis
whereas rheumatoid

361
00:19:48,330 --> 00:19:51,970
arthritis shows
increased inflammation,

362
00:19:52,130 --> 00:19:56,890
anti-CCP, increased
RF, ESR, CRP

363
00:19:56,890 --> 00:19:58,250
and the decreased
complement.

364
00:19:59,610 --> 00:20:02,330
Osteoarthritis is
characterized by joint

365
00:20:02,330 --> 00:20:05,630
space narrowing,
osteophytes, joint mice,

366
00:20:05,630 --> 00:20:09,130
subchondral sclerosis and
so-called eburonation,

367
00:20:09,310 --> 00:20:11,350
whereas the
rheumatoid arthritis

368
00:20:11,350 --> 00:20:13,130
we have panos formation.

369
00:20:13,310 --> 00:20:17,660
There is no other
extra-articular

370
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:19,810
feature in
osteoarthritis,

371
00:20:19,910 --> 00:20:22,100
whereas the rheumatoid
arthritis is

372
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:25,370
associated with
numerous extra-articular

373
00:20:25,370 --> 00:20:28,710
features, such as
rheumatoid nodules,

374
00:20:28,710 --> 00:20:31,610
pleuritis, pericarditis,
Felty syndrome,

375
00:20:31,610 --> 00:20:34,890
as we just described
previously.

376
00:20:38,890 --> 00:20:41,910
Juvenile idiopathic
arthritis represents

377
00:20:41,910 --> 00:20:43,890
a heterogeneous
group of disorders of

378
00:20:43,890 --> 00:20:47,110
unknown cause, which
develops before 16

379
00:20:47,110 --> 00:20:49,510
years of age and lasts
at least six weeks.

380
00:20:50,030 --> 00:20:52,840
The patient presents
with lococytosis,

381
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:55,090
thrombocytosis,
and anemia.

382
00:20:55,850 --> 00:20:58,750
The patient is seropositive
for antinuclear

383
00:20:58,750 --> 00:21:02,510
antibody, and the ESR
and CRP are increased.

384
00:21:02,510 --> 00:21:06,750
However, the pathogenesis
remains unknown.

385
00:21:06,750 --> 00:21:08,790
There might be some
association with certain

386
00:21:08,790 --> 00:21:12,630
HLA and PT-PN22 gene
variants, but nothing

387
00:21:12,630 --> 00:21:14,770
is well established
at the present time.

388
00:21:15,150 --> 00:21:18,450
They will develop
daily spiking fevers,

389
00:21:19,310 --> 00:21:22,030
a salmon pink macular
rash, and arthritis

390
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:24,650
