least two joints.

391
00:21:24,650 --> 00:21:27,530
There is anterior
uveitis, but the patient

392
00:21:27,530 --> 00:21:30,770
does not develop usually
rheumatoid nodules.

393
00:21:30,770 --> 00:21:34,590
The long-term prognosis
is variable, as many

394
00:21:34,590 --> 00:21:37,090
patients may have
other chronic diseases.

395
00:21:37,230 --> 00:21:39,510
However, about
10% will develop

396
00:21:39,510 --> 00:21:41,430
serious functional
disability.

397
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:45,090
The therapy is
represented by NSAIDs,

398
00:21:45,090 --> 00:21:49,010
steroids, methotrexate,
and TNF inhibitors.

399
00:21:52,170 --> 00:21:56,130
Let's talk now about
defects in hormones

400
00:21:56,130 --> 00:21:58,590
and signal
transduction proteins.

401
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:01,670
Acrondoplasia,
this is the most

402
00:22:01,670 --> 00:22:03,470
common skeletal dysplasia

403
00:22:03,470 --> 00:22:05,590
and a major cause
of dwarfism.

404
00:22:07,210 --> 00:22:09,930
Thanatodorphic
dysplasia, on the

405
00:22:09,930 --> 00:22:11,610
other hand, is the
most common lethal

406
00:22:11,610 --> 00:22:14,170
form of dwarfism,
and it's seen

407
00:22:14,170 --> 00:22:19,590
in one every 20
,000 life newborns.

408
00:22:19,730 --> 00:22:24,110
This is caused by
if GFR3 gain of

409
00:22:24,110 --> 00:22:26,550
function mutation,
which is different

410
00:22:26,550 --> 00:22:28,920
than those that
cause acrondoplasia.

411
00:22:31,180 --> 00:22:33,130
This patient
presents with

412
00:22:33,130 --> 00:22:35,850
disproportionately
short micromelic limbs,

413
00:22:35,950 --> 00:22:37,390
frontal bossing,

414
00:22:37,730 --> 00:22:40,850
