which makes sclera

517
00:28:13,530 --> 00:28:15,870
translucent with
partial visualization

518
00:28:15,870 --> 00:28:18,910
of the underlying
choroidal veins.

519
00:28:19,350 --> 00:28:21,930
There are also
dental imperfections,

520
00:28:21,930 --> 00:28:23,230
the teeth are small

521
00:28:23,230 --> 00:28:26,410
mishapen and blue
-yellow in color.

522
00:28:26,780 --> 00:28:28,410
All of these
are secondary

523
00:28:28,410 --> 00:28:30,370
to a dentin deficiency.

524
00:28:32,930 --> 00:28:36,110
Osteoporosis. This is
defined as osteopenia

525
00:28:36,170 --> 00:28:38,510
or a decreased bone
mass severe enough

526
00:28:38,510 --> 00:28:40,170
to increase the
risk of fracture.

527
00:28:40,730 --> 00:28:43,390
On X-ray, there is
bone mass at least

528
00:28:43,390 --> 00:28:45,970
2.5 standard
deviations below main

529
00:28:45,970 --> 00:28:48,710
peak bone mass
for a young adult.

530
00:28:48,710 --> 00:28:51,110
The most common
forms of osteoporosis

531
00:28:51,110 --> 00:28:53,610
are senile and
postmenopausal.

532
00:28:54,670 --> 00:28:57,750
In senile osteoporosis,
there is a diminished

533
00:28:57,750 --> 00:29:00,510
ability to make
bone as a result of

534
00:29:00,510 --> 00:29:02,810
reduced proliferative
and biosynthetic

535
00:29:02,810 --> 00:29:06,510
capacity and a reduced
response to growth

536
00:29:06,510 --> 00:29:11,590
factors released by
osteoblasts. Also in

537
00:29:11,590 --> 00:29:13,250
old age there is
decreased physical

538
00:29:13,250 --> 00:29:16,690
activity which leads
to less bone formation.

539
00:29:17,590 --> 00:29:22,510
The first image
represents a section

540
00:29:22,510 --> 00:29:25,230
of a normal
vertebral body with

541
00:29:25,230 --> 00:29:27,610
dense and well
-calcified trabeculate.

542
00:29:28,610 --> 00:29:31,850
On the right side you
see an osteoporotic

543
00:29:31,850 --> 00:29:33,830
vertebra with
ratification of

544
00:29:33,830 --> 00:29:36,170
trabeculate which
weakens the mechanical

545
00:29:36,170 --> 00:29:38,450
properties of the
vertebral body.

546
00:29:41,930 --> 00:29:45,830
Postmenopausal osteoporosis.
After menopause

547
00:29:45,830 --> 00:29:48,390
up to two percent
of cortical bone and

548
00:29:48,390 --> 00:29:50,270
nine percent of
cancellous bone might be

549
00:29:50,270 --> 00:29:52,840
lost per year due to
estrogen deficiency.

550
00:29:53,550 --> 00:29:56,570
Estrogen deficiency
determines

551
00:29:56,570 --> 00:29:59,090
both both formation
and resorption

552
00:29:59,090 --> 00:30:01,450
but resorption dominates.

553
00:30:02,750 --> 00:30:05,710
Estrogen loss is
associated with an

554
00:30:05,710 --> 00:30:07,410
increased secretion
of inflammatory

555
00:30:07,410 --> 00:30:11,430
cytokines release For
example, IL-6, TNF,

556
00:30:11,430 --> 00:30:14,450
and IL-1 by innate
immune cells in

557
00:30:14,450 --> 00:30:18,010
blood and marrow via
unknown mechanisms

558
00:30:19,030 --> 00:30:22,670
This results in increases
and decreases in

559
00:30:22,670 --> 00:30:26,470
rank ligand and OPG,
respectively Which

560
00:30:26,470 --> 00:30:29,190
stimulate osteoclast
recruitment and activity

561
00:30:30,470 --> 00:30:32,550
Histologically
normal bone

562
00:30:32,550 --> 00:30:35,010
is decreased in quantity.

563
00:30:35,270 --> 00:30:37,290
The entire skeleton
is affected,

564
00:30:37,290 --> 00:30:38,670
but certain
bones might be

565
00:30:38,670 --> 00:30:41,130
severely affected
than others.

566
00:30:42,290 --> 00:30:44,710
Postmenopausal
osteoporosis affects

567
00:30:44,710 --> 00:30:47,130
mainly bones or
portions of bones

568
00:30:47,130 --> 00:30:49,190
with increased
surface area, for

569
00:30:49,190 --> 00:30:52,490
example vertebral
bodies. Trabecular

570
00:30:52,490 --> 00:30:56,130
plates become
perforated and thinned,

571
00:30:56,490 --> 00:31:00,870
the interconnections
are loose and this leads

572
00:31:00,870 --> 00:31:04,470
to microfactors and
at the vertebral level

573
00:31:04,470 --> 00:31:07,610
we will have in time
vertebral collapse.

574
00:31:11,650 --> 00:31:14,610
In conclusion, some
genetic factors

575
00:31:14,610 --> 00:31:17,970
associated with
inadequate physical

576
00:31:17,970 --> 00:31:21,010
activity and poor
nutrition may lead to

577
00:31:21,010 --> 00:31:24,970
peak bone mass loss
and osteoporosis.

578
00:31:25,070 --> 00:31:29,350
In menopause,
we have also

579
00:31:29,350 --> 00:31:31,010
decreased serum estrogen,

580
00:31:31,010 --> 00:31:34,910
increased IL-1, IL
-6, and TNF levels.

581
00:31:35,350 --> 00:31:37,890
There is an
increased expression

582
00:31:38,330 --> 00:31:40,750
of rank and
rank ligand and

583
00:31:40,750 --> 00:31:42,770
increased
osteoplast activity.

584
00:31:43,110 --> 00:31:47,190
In aging, we have a
decreased replicative

585
00:31:47,190 --> 00:31:50,550
activity of
osteoprogenitor cells, a

586
00:31:50,550 --> 00:31:53,580
decreased synthetic
activity of osteoblasts

587
00:31:53,580 --> 00:31:56,070
and a decreased
biologic activity

588
00:31:56,070 --> 00:31:59,430
of matrix-bound growth
factors associated

589
00:31:59,430 --> 00:32:01,930
with reduced physical
activity, which

590
00:32:01,930 --> 00:32:04,230
ultimately would
lead to osteoporosis.

591
00:32:05,010 --> 00:32:07,890
There is about 10
million Americans

592
00:32:07,890 --> 00:32:09,910
and 200 million
people worldwide

593
00:32:09,910 --> 00:32:13,950
with osteoporosis
and 1.5 million

594
00:32:13,950 --> 00:32:17,050
osteoportic fracture
occur each year.

595
00:32:17,070 --> 00:32:20,310
The male to female
ratio is 1 to 4.

596
00:32:20,550 --> 00:32:23,310
Men have higher
prevalence of secondary

597
00:32:23,310 --> 00:32:28,690
osteoporosis
about 60%. So the

598
00:32:28,690 --> 00:32:31,330
most common location
for the fractures

599
00:32:31,330 --> 00:32:33,930
is represented by
the vertebral body

600
00:32:33,930 --> 00:32:35,910
followed by the
hip and the wrist.

601
00:32:36,350 --> 00:32:38,830
The A vertebral
body fracture is a

602
00:32:38,830 --> 00:32:40,710
compression
fracture, especially

603
00:32:40,710 --> 00:32:42,610
in the thoracic
and lumbar region.

604
00:32:42,830 --> 00:32:46,370
It is painful and when
multiple can cause

605
00:32:46,370 --> 00:32:49,290
significant loss of
height and deformities,

606
00:32:49,290 --> 00:32:51,790
lumbar lordosis
and kyphoscoliosis.

607
00:32:53,310 --> 00:32:57,210
There is also a very
important fracture,

608
00:32:57,210 --> 00:32:58,650
the femoral neck
fracture, which

609
00:32:58,650 --> 00:33:02,870
leads to loss of
mobility and high

610
00:33:02,870 --> 00:33:05,010
mortality, especially
in the elderly with

611
00:33:05,010 --> 00:33:07,110
other chronic
conditions associated.

612
00:33:07,630 --> 00:33:09,430
Also very serious is the

613
00:33:09,430 --> 00:33:10,810
distal radius fracture,

614
00:33:11,370 --> 00:33:13,990
which in elderly
patients can heal

615
00:33:13,990 --> 00:33:15,510
with a great deal
of difficulty.

616
00:33:16,170 --> 00:33:19,370
This radiological image
shows the anterior

617
00:33:19,370 --> 00:33:21,730
posterior radiograph
of the proximal part

618
00:33:21,730 --> 00:33:24,980
of femur of a patient
who had osteoporosis,

619
00:33:24,980 --> 00:33:27,710
showing a fracture
of the femoral neck.

620
00:33:36,480 --> 00:33:39,180
Osteoporosis is
detected in plain X-rays

621
00:33:39,180 --> 00:33:42,420
when 30 to 40% of
bone mass is lost.

622
00:33:43,420 --> 00:33:47,540
Usually the diagnosis
is done by a

623
00:33:47,540 --> 00:33:49,900
DIXA scan. DIXA is
the abbreviation

624
00:33:49,900 --> 00:33:53,030
for Dual Energy X
-ray Absorciometry

625
00:33:53,900 --> 00:33:56,240
and is recommended
for all

626
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:58,600
women more than
65 years of age.

627
00:33:58,620 --> 00:34:02,240
This test provides
a T-score which

628
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:06,140
basically compares
the bone density of

629
00:34:06,140 --> 00:34:08,300
the patient to a
healthy 30-year-old.

630
00:34:08,840 --> 00:34:12,520
A score of less
or equal with

631
00:34:12,520 --> 00:34:15,300
minus 2.5 indicates
osteoporosis.

632
00:34:15,480 --> 00:34:20,180
A score between minus
2.5 and minus 1 is

633
00:34:20,180 --> 00:34:23,060
diagnostic for osteopenia,
while a score of

634
00:34:23,060 --> 00:34:27,620
at least minus 1
suggests a healthy bone.

635
00:34:28,280 --> 00:34:32,340
These patients should
be prescribed diet

636
00:34:32,340 --> 00:34:34,840
-reaching calcium and
vitamin D supplements,

637
00:34:35,020 --> 00:34:37,260
weight-bearing
exercises, and

638
00:34:37,260 --> 00:34:39,600
bifosphonates, which
are known to reduce

639
00:34:39,600 --> 00:34:44,140
osteoclast activity
and bone resorption

640
00:34:48,890 --> 00:34:50,610
Osteopetrosis

641
00:34:51,400 --> 00:34:53,210
Osteopetrosis
represents a group of

642
00:34:53,210 --> 00:34:55,510
rare genetic diseases
characterized by

643
00:34:55,510 --> 00:34:57,910
reduced bone resorption
due to deficient

644
00:34:57,910 --> 00:34:59,930
osteoclast development
or function

645
00:35:00,380 --> 00:35:02,710
This ultimately
results in diffuse

646
00:35:02,710 --> 00:35:04,770
symmetrical
skeletal sclerosis.

647
00:35:05,520 --> 00:35:07,470
I would like to
highlight that the

648
00:35:07,470 --> 00:35:09,470
term osteopetrosis
would imply

649
00:35:09,470 --> 00:35:12,850
something hard,
stone-like. However,

650
00:35:13,410 --> 00:35:15,530
bones in these
patients are

651
00:35:15,530 --> 00:35:17,350
brittle and
fracture easily.

652
00:35:19,290 --> 00:35:22,530
Osteopetrosis represents
several variants

653
00:35:22,530 --> 00:35:25,510
based on mode of
inheritance as well as

654
00:35:25,510 --> 00:35:29,210
severity of clinical
findings most mutations in

655
00:35:29,210 --> 00:35:32,170
osteopetrosis interfere
with acidification

656
00:35:32,190 --> 00:35:34,570
of the osteoclast
resorption pit which

657
00:35:34,570 --> 00:35:36,870
is needed for the
solution of calcium

658
00:35:36,870 --> 00:35:39,450
hydroxyapatite within
the bone matrix

659
00:35:39,990 --> 00:35:43,670
these patients
present in fact with

660
00:35:43,670 --> 00:35:46,330
a mutation in
carbonic anhydrase 2

661
00:35:46,570 --> 00:35:49,310
which is associated
with inability to

662
00:35:49,310 --> 00:35:52,850
generate acidic
environment necessary for

663
00:35:52,850 --> 00:35:56,370
osteoclast function. The
osteoclasts are defective,

664
00:35:56,370 --> 00:35:58,890
they cannot resolve
bone properly and

665
00:35:58,930 --> 00:36:01,030
this leads to dense but

666
00:36:01,030 --> 00:36:02,710
fracture prone bones.

667
00:36:03,750 --> 00:36:05,990
Ultimately the
bone fills marrow

668
00:36:05,990 --> 00:36:09,030
space leading to
pancytopenia and

669
00:36:09,030 --> 00:36:11,310
extra medullary
hematopoiesis.

670
00:36:16,110 --> 00:36:19,130
Radiology in this
patient would reveal a

671
00:36:19,130 --> 00:36:22,950
symmetric sclerosis, the
so-called bone in bone

672
00:36:22,950 --> 00:36:26,750
pattern. This is
determined by a bone which

673
00:36:26,750 --> 00:36:30,450
is not remodeled but
tends to be woven

674
00:36:30,450 --> 00:36:34,570
rather than lamellar.
The long bones have no

675
00:36:34,570 --> 00:36:38,590
medullary cavity
because the osteoclast

676
00:36:38,590 --> 00:36:42,430
activity is deficient and
they will present with

677
00:36:42,430 --> 00:36:45,370
the so-called Ehlenmeyer
flask deformity.

678
00:36:46,090 --> 00:36:49,310
Also in this patient
we might see a

679
00:36:49,310 --> 00:36:52,570
narrow neural
foraminum and various

680
00:36:52,570 --> 00:36:55,010
types of cranial
nerve compressions

681
00:36:55,010 --> 00:36:57,650
associated with
pulses and deafness.

682
00:36:58,670 --> 00:37:00,970
There is an increased
risk of fractures

683
00:37:00,970 --> 00:37:03,210
especially in the lower
extremity followed

684
00:37:03,210 --> 00:37:06,150
by upper extremity
and axial skeleton.

685
00:37:06,970 --> 00:37:11,430
A severe infantile
osteopetrosis is usually

686
00:37:11,430 --> 00:37:14,650
autosomal recessive
transmitted and is

687
00:37:14,790 --> 00:37:19,370
evident in utero or
soon after birth. The

688
00:37:19,370 --> 00:37:21,770
autosomal dominant
forms are milder and

689
00:37:21,770 --> 00:37:24,270
might not be detected
until adolescence.

690
00:37:25,350 --> 00:37:30,630
Therapy is with bone
marrow transplant and

691
00:37:30,630 --> 00:37:34,630
is potentially curative
as by this procedure

692
00:37:34,630 --> 00:37:40,050
we provide the patient
with hematopoietic

693
00:37:40,050 --> 00:37:44,010
precursors for the
functional osteoclasts.

694
00:37:45,250 --> 00:37:48,230
Malasia and rickets
represent metabolic

695
00:37:48,230 --> 00:37:51,750
entities determined by
defective mineralization

696
00:37:51,750 --> 00:37:54,730
of osteoid or cartilaginous
growth plates.

697
00:37:55,510 --> 00:37:57,050
They are
associated with a

698
00:37:57,050 --> 00:37:59,330
low vitamin D,
low sunlight

699
00:37:59,450 --> 00:38:01,930
and kidney disease.

700
00:38:02,770 --> 00:38:05,990
Osteomalasia is seen in
adults with defective

701
00:38:05,990 --> 00:38:08,790
mineralization of
osteoid, while rickets

702
00:38:08,790 --> 00:38:12,030
is diagnosed in
children with effective

703
00:38:12,030 --> 00:38:14,630
mineralization of
cartilaginous growth plates.

704
00:38:15,190 --> 00:38:19,430
The incidence is 1
in 1000 in the US.

705
00:38:19,730 --> 00:38:25,290
It is therefore fairly
low and is due to a

706
00:38:25,290 --> 00:38:28,070
dairy product fortification
with vitamin D

707
00:38:28,070 --> 00:38:30,650
and adequate sunlight
in most of the people.

708
00:38:31,130 --> 00:38:34,750
The laboratory studies
will show a decreased

709
00:38:34,750 --> 00:38:37,810
vitamin D, decreased
calcium absorption,

710
00:38:37,810 --> 00:38:41,550
increased PTH and
decreased phosphates.

711
00:38:42,110 --> 00:38:45,430
The osteobloids are
hyperactive and there

712
00:38:45,430 --> 00:38:47,930
is an increase in
alkaline phosphatase.

713
00:38:48,110 --> 00:38:51,320
The therapy is represented
by administration

714
00:38:51,320 --> 00:38:54,810
of large doses of
vitamin D, more

715
00:38:54,810 --> 00:38:57,890
than 1,000 international
units per day.

716
00:39:01,970 --> 00:39:05,510
Osteomalacia is
associated with loser

717
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:08,330
zone which is an
insufficiency fracture

718
00:39:08,330 --> 00:39:10,690
seen at the axillary
border of the

719
00:39:10,690 --> 00:39:13,850
scapula, the rib
or posterior ulna.

720
00:39:14,270 --> 00:39:18,910
In rickets there is
epiphyseal widening

721
00:39:18,910 --> 00:39:22,090
and metaphyseal
cupping or fraying. The

722
00:39:22,090 --> 00:39:25,510
patients present with
genuvarum or bow legs

723
00:39:25,790 --> 00:39:30,890
and rachytic rosary
which represents osteoid

724
00:39:30,890 --> 00:39:33,350
deposition at the
costochondral junction.

725
00:39:38,690 --> 00:39:39,850
Patriot's disease.

726
00:39:40,210 --> 00:39:43,710
Patriot's disease
is associated

727
00:39:43,710 --> 00:39:45,130
with increase by disorder

728
00:39:45,130 --> 00:39:47,550
structurally and
sound bone mass.

729
00:39:47,850 --> 00:39:50,650
There are three
sequential phases.

730
00:39:51,390 --> 00:39:54,550
An initial osteolytic
stage which is

731
00:39:54,550 --> 00:39:57,770
followed by a mixed
osteoclastic-osteoblastic

732
00:39:57,770 --> 00:40:02,350
stage and ultimately
by a burnout

733
00:40:02,350 --> 00:40:05,230
quiescent osteoskeleotic
stage in which

734
00:40:05,230 --> 00:40:07,890
the osteoblast
activity predominates.

735
00:40:08,770 --> 00:40:11,330
Oftentimes it
presents in late

736
00:40:11,330 --> 00:40:13,490
adulthood and
becomes progressively

737
00:40:13,490 --> 00:40:15,610
more common with
increasing age.

738
00:40:15,810 --> 00:40:19,050
It is relatively
common in Caucasians in

739
00:40:19,050 --> 00:40:22,030
England, France, Austria,
regions of Germany,

740
00:40:22,510 --> 00:40:25,850
Australia, New Zealand
and US. It is very

741
00:40:25,850 --> 00:40:29,190
rare in Scandinavia,
China, Japan and Africa.

742
00:40:29,550 --> 00:40:31,810
The exact incident
is not known

743
00:40:31,810 --> 00:40:34,330
because of many
asymptomatic patients.

744
00:40:34,830 --> 00:40:37,570
About 1% of the
US population

745
00:40:37,570 --> 00:40:39,570
more than 40
years of age is

746
00:40:39,570 --> 00:40:42,110
thought to have
a Pages disease.

747
00:40:44,070 --> 00:40:47,170
The major cause of
Page's disease is

748
00:40:47,170 --> 00:40:49,670
unknown. However, there
is evidence of both

749
00:40:49,670 --> 00:40:52,070
genetic and environmental
contributions.

750
00:40:53,190 --> 00:40:56,090
Approximately 50%
of familiar Page's

751
00:40:56,090 --> 00:40:59,250
disease and 10% of
sporadic cases are

752
00:40:59,250 --> 00:41:03,010
associated with
mutations in the SQSTM1

753
00:41:03,010 --> 00:41:06,750
gene, which increases
the NFKB activity,

754
00:41:06,750 --> 00:41:10,630
enhancing osteoclast
activity as well.

755
00:41:11,090 --> 00:41:14,030
Some studies suggest
chronic infection

756
00:41:14,030 --> 00:41:17,150
of osteoclast
precursors by measles or

757
00:41:17,150 --> 00:41:20,610
other RNA viruses as
major contributors.

758
00:41:21,210 --> 00:41:22,870
As mentioned, there are

759
00:41:22,870 --> 00:41:25,270
three pathogenic stages.

760
00:41:25,450 --> 00:41:28,610
The osteolytic stage
is characterized by

761
00:41:28,610 --> 00:41:31,320
increased osteoclastic
activity and bone

762
00:41:31,320 --> 00:41:34,050
resorption. This is
followed by a mixed

763
00:41:34,050 --> 00:41:37,170
stage in which there
is an increase in

764
00:41:37,170 --> 00:41:39,370
both the activity
of osteoclast and

765
00:41:39,370 --> 00:41:43,810
osteoblasts. During this
stage we see resorption

766
00:41:43,810 --> 00:41:46,390
and compensatory
bone reformation.

767
00:41:46,990 --> 00:41:50,250
The osteosclerotic or
the burnout phase is

768
00:41:50,250 --> 00:41:53,270
characterized by
increased number and

769
00:41:53,270 --> 00:41:56,330
activity of osteoblasts
with bone formation.

770
00:41:56,890 --> 00:41:58,950
Sometime all three phases

771
00:41:58,950 --> 00:42:01,110
might coexist
in a given bone.

772
00:42:03,970 --> 00:42:05,710
Histology varies over

773
00:42:05,710 --> 00:42:07,130
time and across sites,

